    Show user roles without associated users in the user table in the ACL… (#7540)
    
    …s in the admin ui. Fixes
    https://github.com/opencast/admin-interface/issues/1361
    
    If you have user role sanitization off, the admin ui will display roles
    in the ACL tab in two categories, "users" and "roles and groups".
    Currently, the definition of a role for the users category is that there
    should exist a user for the username after the user role prefix, in
    Opencast or otherwise. E.g. if the role is ROLE_USER_GEORGE, it will be
    sorted in the users category only if there is a user "george" in
    Opencast or if "george" can be provided by a user provider.
    
    This patch changes the definition. Now, a role only needs to start with
    the user role prefix to be sorted into the users category. E.g. the role
    ROLE_USER_GEORGE would now always show up in the users category, no
    matter if such a user actually exists.
    
    This should be more in line with expected behaviour, and help with
    certain use cases where a user does not yet exist (meaning it should
    help with whatever ILIAS is doing).
    The downside is that now strings such as ROLE_USER_GEORGE can appear
    next to usernames like "Theodore" in the users category, which may be
    strange to some users.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Make sure to set `sanitize=false` in
    `etc/org.opencastproject.userdirectory.UserIdRoleProvider.cfg`.
    If you don't have an ILIAS to test with, you can define custom user
    roles for non-existing users in the `etc/custom.properties` under
    `org.opencastproject.security.custom.roles`.
    
    
